      <p class="_abstract">As a cluster administrator, you can remove an egress firewall from a project to remove all restrictions on network traffic from the project that leaves the OpenShift Container Platform cluster.</p>
      <h2 id="nw-egress-firewall-delete_removing-egress-firewall-ovn" class="group scroll-mt-20">Removing an EgressFirewall CR<a href="#nw-egress-firewall-delete_removing-egress-firewall-ovn" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">As a cluster administrator, you can remove an egress firewall from a project.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>A cluster using the OVN-Kubernetes network plugin.</li>
      <li>Install the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You must log in to the cluster as a cluster administrator.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Find the name of the <code>EgressFirewall</code> CR for the project. Replace <code>&lt;project&gt;</code> with the name of the project.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get egressfirewall -n <project>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>EgressFirewall</code> CR by entering the following command. Replace <code>&lt;project&gt;</code> with the name of the project and <code>&lt;name&gt;</code> with the name of the object.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete -n <project> egressfirewall <name>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
